        ('mth11a-01-mcq-0023', 1, 'In a classroom grouping exercise, four sets are recorded with consecutive labels. For A={7, 8, 9}, B={9, 10, 11}, C={11, 12, 13}, D={13, 14, 15}, what is the required union B∪C∪D?', '{9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15}', '{9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15}', '{7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15}', '{9}', 'b', 1, 'For a union, collect every distinct element from each named set once.', 'List the elements appearing in the named sets and remove duplicates. The required union is {9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15}. The distractors represent combining all four sets, taking an intersection where applicable, or forming a different union. Wrong-option audit: Option A: using the wrong union scope.  Option C: taking an intersection.  Option D: using a different set combination.'),
        ('mth11a-01-mcq-0024', 1, 'For A={10, 11, 12}, B={12, 13, 14}, C={14, 15, 16}, D={16, 17, 18}, what is the required union A∪B?', '{10, 11, 12, 13, 14}', '{10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18}', '{12}', '{12, 13, 14, 16, 17, 18}', 'a', 1, 'For a union, collect every distinct element from each named set once.', 'List the elements appearing in the named sets and remove duplicates. The required union is {10, 11, 12, 13, 14}. The distractors represent combining all four sets, taking an intersection where applicable, or forming a different union. Wrong-option audit: Option B: using the wrong union scope.  Option C: taking an intersection.  Option D: using a different set combination.'),
