        ('mth11a-03-mcq-0042', 3, 'If z₁=4-2i, z₂=-1+3i, z₃=5+i, find 3z₁ − (2z₂ + 1z₃).', '1-9i', '19-11i', '5-i', '9-13i', 'd', 2, 'Distribute the outside subtraction, then combine real and imaginary parts.', 'Real part = 3(4)−2(-1)−1(5)=9; imaginary part = 3(-2)−2(3)−1(1)=-13. Hence 9-13i.
