        ('mth11a-03-mcq-0043', 3, 'If z₁=-6+5i, z₂=2-4i, z₃=-3-i, find 2z₁ − (3z₂ + 4z₃).', '-6+26i', '-30+18i', '21i', '6+2i', 'a', 2, 'Distribute the outside subtraction, then combine real and imaginary parts.', 'Real part = 2(-6)−3(2)−4(-3)=-6; imaginary part = 2(5)−3(-4)−4(-1)=26. Hence -6+26i.
