        ('mth11a-03-mcq-0044', 3, 'If z₁=8-3i, z₂=4+2i, z₃=-2+6i, find 4z₁ − (1z₂ + 3z₃).', '34-32i', '42-28i', '10-23i', '22+4i', 'a', 2, 'Distribute the outside subtraction, then combine real and imaginary parts.', 'Real part = 4(8)−1(4)−3(-2)=34; imaginary part = 4(-3)−1(2)−3(6)=-32. Hence 34-32i.
