        ('mth11a-03-mcq-0045', 3, 'If z₁=-5-i, z₂=3+5i, z₃=2-2i, find 3z₁ − (4z₂ + 2z₃).', '-23-27i', '-7+21i', '-31-19i', '-21-17i', 'c', 2, 'Distribute the outside subtraction, then combine real and imaginary parts.', 'Real part = 3(-5)−4(3)−2(2)=-31; imaginary part = 3(-1)−4(5)−2(-2)=-19. Hence -31-19i.
