        ('mth11a-03-mcq-0046', 3, 'If z₁=6+7i, z₂=-2+i, z₃=4-5i, find 2z₁ − (2z₂ + 3z₃).', '-2+20i', '-4+31i', '4+27i', '28-3i', 'c', 2, 'Distribute the outside subtraction, then combine real and imaginary parts.', 'Real part = 2(6)−2(-2)−3(4)=4; imaginary part = 2(7)−2(1)−3(-5)=27. Hence 4+27i.
