        ('mth11a-04-mcq-0061', 4, 'In a G.P., t₃=8 and t₆=64. Which formula gives its nth term?', 'tₙ = 2(1/2)^(n−1)', 'tₙ = 8(2)^(n−1)', 'tₙ = 2(2)^(n−1)', 'tₙ = 2(2)^n', 'c', 2, 'Use t₆/t₃=r³ and then t₃=ar².', 't₆/t₃=8=r³, so r=2. Then a=t₃/r²=2. Therefore tₙ=arⁿ⁻¹=tₙ = 2(2)^(n−1).
