Option D results from using n instead of n−1.'),
        ('mth11a-04-mcq-0062', 4, 'In a G.P., t₃=3/4 and t₆=3/32. Which formula gives its nth term?', 'tₙ = 3(2)^(n−1)', 'tₙ = 3(1/2)^(n−1)', 'tₙ = 3(1/2)^n', 'tₙ = 3/4(1/2)^(n−1)', 'b', 2, 'Use t₆/t₃=r³ and then t₃=ar².', 't₆/t₃=1/8=r³, so r=1/2. Then a=t₃/r²=3. Therefore tₙ=arⁿ⁻¹=tₙ = 3(1/2)^(n−1).
