        ('mth11a-05-mcq-0171', 5, 'Reduce the equation 2x - y - 3 = 0 into normal form.', '(2/sqrt(5))x + (-1/sqrt(5))y = -3/sqrt(5)', '(-1/sqrt(5))x + (2/sqrt(5))y = 3/sqrt(5)', '(2/√5)x + (-1/√5)y = 3/√5', '(2/sqrt(5))x + (1/sqrt(5))y = 3/sqrt(5)', 'c', 3, 'Divide the general equation by √(a²+b²) and match x cosα+y sinα=p.', 'Divide 2x - y - 3 = 0 by √(a²+b²)=√(5) and choose the sign so the right side is the normal distance. This gives (2/√5)x + (-1/√5)y = 3/√5.

