        ('mth11a-05-mcq-0249', 5, 'For the line 9x + 4y - 36 = 0, find its slope, x-intercept, and y-intercept.', 'slope -9/4, x-intercept 4, y-intercept -9', 'slope -9/4, x-intercept -4, y-intercept 9', 'slope -9/4, x-intercept 4, y-intercept 9', 'slope 9/4, x-intercept 4, y-intercept 9', 'c', 2, 'Compare with ax+by+c=0, then use −a/b, −c/a and −c/b.', 'Compare with ax+by+c=0. Then slope=−a/b=-9/4, x-intercept=−c/a=4, and y-intercept=−c/b=9. Thus slope -9/4, x-intercept 4, y-intercept 9.

