        ('mth11a-05-mcq-0276', 5, 'Find the equations of the lines through the origin that make an angle of 45° with the line having slope 1/2.', 'y = -3x and y = -1/3x', 'y = 3x and y = -1/3x', 'y = 3x and y = 1/3x', 'y = 3x + 1 and y = -1/3x', 'b', 3, 'Use the angle formula with tan45°=1 and solve for the unknown slope.', 'For a required slope m, tan45°=|(m−1/2)/(1+m(1/2))|=1. Solving the two cases gives m=3 and m=-1/3. Since both lines pass through the origin, their equations are y = 3x and y = -1/3x.

