        ('mth11a-05-mcq-0277', 5, 'Find the equations of the lines through the origin that make an angle of 45° with the line having slope 1/3.', 'y = -2x and y = -1/2x', 'y = 2x + 1 and y = -1/2x', 'y = 2x and y = 1/2x', 'y = 2x and y = -1/2x', 'd', 3, 'Use the angle formula with tan45°=1 and solve for the unknown slope.', 'For a required slope m, tan45°=|(m−1/3)/(1+m(1/3))|=1. Solving the two cases gives m=2 and m=-1/2. Since both lines pass through the origin, their equations are y = 2x and y = -1/2x.

