        ('mth11a-05-mcq-0279', 5, 'Find the equations of the lines through the origin that make an angle of 45° with the line having slope 2/3.', 'y = 5x and y = 1/5x', 'y = -5x and y = -1/5x', 'y = 5x and y = -1/5x', 'y = 5x + 1 and y = -1/5x', 'c', 3, 'Use the angle formula with tan45°=1 and solve for the unknown slope.', 'For a required slope m, tan45°=|(m−2/3)/(1+m(2/3))|=1. Solving the two cases gives m=5 and m=-1/5. Since both lines pass through the origin, their equations are y = 5x and y = -1/5x.

