        ('mth11a-06-mcq-0036', 6, 'Determine whether 1x + 1y + (-2) = 0; 2x + -1y + (-7) = 0; 3x + 2y + (-7) = 0 are consistent.', 'No common solution', 'Consistent', 'Parallel only', 'Not consistent', 'b', 2, 'Form the 3×3 determinant from a, b and c.', 'The determinant of the coefficient-constant rows is 0, so the necessary consistency condition is satisfied. Option A: confusing the determinant test. Option C: using an unrelated slope conclusion. Option D: assuming a nonzero determinant.'),
