        ('mth11a-07-mcq-0108', 7, 'Evaluate lim(x→8) [(1/x − 1/8)/(x−8)].', '-1/64', '-1/9', '1/64', '-1/11', 'a', 2, 'Combine the two fractions first so that x−a appears as a factor.', '1/x−1/8=(8−x)/(8x)=−(x−8)/(8x). Cancel x−8; the limit is −1/8² = -1/64. Option B: used a+1 instead of a. Option C: sign error after rewriting a−x. Option D: forgot an additional factor in the denominator.'),
        ('mth11a-07-mcq-0109', 7, 'Evaluate lim(x→9) [(1/x − 1/9)/(x−9)].', '1/81', '-1/10', '-1/81', '-1/12', 'c', 2, 'Combine the two fractions first so that x−a appears as a factor.', '1/x−1/9=(9−x)/(9x)=−(x−9)/(9x). Cancel x−9; the limit is −1/9² = -1/81. Option A: sign error after rewriting a−x. Option B: used a+1 instead of a. Option D: forgot an additional factor in the denominator.'),
        ('mth11a-07-mcq-0110', 7, 'Evaluate lim(x→10) [(1/x − 1/10)/(x−10)].', '-1/13', '-1/100', '1/100', '-1/11', 'b', 2, 'Combine the two fractions first so that x−a appears as a factor.', '1/x−1/10=(10−x)/(10x)=−(x−10)/(10x). Cancel x−10; the limit is −1/10² = -1/100. Option A: forgot an additional factor in the denominator. Option C: sign error after rewriting a−x. Option D: used a+1 instead of a.'),
        ('mth11a-07-mcq-0111', 7, 'Evaluate lim(z→0) [(√(1+z) − √(1−z))/z]', '2/√1', '1/√1', '1/1', '-1/√1', 'b', 2, 'Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator, then simplify.', 'Multiplying by √(1+z)+√(1−z) makes the numerator 2z. After cancelling z and taking z→0, the result is 1/√1. Option A: failed to divide by the factor 2. Option C: forgot the square root. Option D: sign error in the conjugate difference.'),
        ('mth11a-07-mcq-0112', 7, 'Evaluate lim(z→0) [(√(2+z) − √(2−z))/z]', '1/√2', '1/2', '-1/√2', '2/√2', 'a', 2, 'Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator, then simplify.', 'Multiplying by √(2+z)+√(2−z) makes the numerator 2z. After cancelling z and taking z→0, the result is 1/√2. Option B: forgot the square root. Option C: sign error in the conjugate difference. Option D: failed to divide by the factor 2.'),
