        ('mth11a-09-mcq-0152', 9, 'Demand D is inversely proportional to the square of price P. If demand is 4 when P=3, find the marginal demand when P=3.', '- \frac{8}{9}', '\frac{8}{3}', '- \frac{8}{3}', '- \frac{4}{3}', 'c', 2, 'Write D=k/P², use the observed pair to find k, then differentiate with respect to P.', 'D=k/P². Since D=4 at P=3, k=4(3)²=36. Thus dD/dP=−2k/P³. At P=3, this becomes - \frac{8}{3}.
